Kind: ablation
Issue: #915
Takes out: O_EXCL from bootlog's open of DIR/boot-N.txt -- the open of the first name succeeds whether or not a file has it, so the second boot on the same disk opens the first boot's file and writes over it from its first byte instead of making boot-2.txt; boot-log-disk-x86_64.sh, booting twice on the same disks, finds no /log/boot-2.txt and boot-1.txt not as the first boot left it
Accel: tcg,kvm
Script: scripts/boot-log-disk-x86_64.sh
Script: --boots
Script: 2
Script: 240
Note: two boots of 240 s each, the -b deadline, as with ext_server in the bundle no quiet census comes; ablate.sh puts --kvm in front under KVM
Expect: boot-log-disk: WRONG -- boot 2: no /log/boot-2.txt

